\ ==== segment-crossings ( segments x z dx dz -- v ) ====

\ The line through the point x z along the direction dx dz crosses the
\ segments, the rows [ x0 z0 x1 z1 ] of an n×4 matrix, at the distances t
\ along it, the point x z + t·(dx dz): a k×1 vector in ascending order. A
\ segment counts when its ends lie on opposite sides of the line, an end on
\ the line counting with the right side, so two segments meeting on the
\ line give one crossing where the outline passes through and none where it
\ only touches.

[ 0 0 4 0  4 0 4 4  4 4 0 4  0 4 0 0 ] 4 4 matrix to square

\ === a square crossed: two distances, in order ===
square 1 2 1 0 segment-crossings matrix>array . cr          \ [ -1 3 ]
square 1 2 -1 0 segment-crossings matrix>array . cr         \ [ -3 1 ]
square 2 0 0 1 segment-crossings matrix>array . cr          \ [ 0 4 ]
square 0 0 1 1 segment-crossings matrix>array . cr          \ [ 0 4 ]
square 1 2 2 0 segment-crossings matrix>array . cr          \ [ -0.5 1.5 ]
clear

\ === a line missing every segment: an empty vector ===
square 0 9 1 0 segment-crossings dim . . cr                 \ 1 0
clear

\ === two segments meeting on the line ===
\ passing through the meeting point: one crossing
[ 0 0 1 1  1 1 2 2 ] 2 4 matrix 0 1 1 0 segment-crossings matrix>array . cr   \ [ 1 ]
\ touching it from below, a peak: none
[ 0 0 1 1  1 1 2 0 ] 2 4 matrix 0 1 1 0 segment-crossings matrix>array . cr   \ [ ]
\ touching it from above, a trough: two at the same place, the parity kept
[ 0 2 1 1  1 1 2 2 ] 2 4 matrix 0 1 1 0 segment-crossings matrix>array . cr   \ [ 1 1 ]
clear

\ === the even-odd test: positive distances due east, odd inside ===
square 2 2 1 0 segment-crossings 0 > sum . cr               \ 1
square 6 2 1 0 segment-crossings 0 > sum . cr               \ 0
clear

\ === errors ===
[ 0 0 1 ] 1 3 matrix 0 0 1 0 segment-crossings              \ (not 4 columns)
square 0 0 0 0 segment-crossings                            \ (zero direction)
"square" 0 0 1 0 segment-crossings                          \ (not a matrix)
square 0 0 1 "east" segment-crossings                       \ (a string direction)
